    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN nodes (numbered 111 to NNN) rooted at node 111.\n\nNode iii has value Ai(1≤Au≤109)A_i(1 \\leq A_u \\leq 10^9)Ai​(1≤Au​≤109) associated to it.\n\nYou will receive QQQ queries, each containing two nodes uuu and vvv. For each query:\n\n\nFirst swap values AuA_uAu​ and AvA_vAv​ ;\nSuppose PxP_xPx​ denotes the array containing the values of all nodes in the subtree of xxx (including node xxx) in non-decreasing order.\nSuppose array LLL is the lexicographically smallest array among P1,P2,…PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots P_NP1​,P2​,…PN​.\nFind the sum of all u(1≤u≤N)u(1 \\leq u \\leq N)u(1≤u≤N) such that Pu=LP_u = LPu​=L.\nNote that the swaps are persistent between queries. In other words, the answer for a query is dependent on the swaps made during earlier queries.\n\nNote that an array SSS is said to be lexicographically smaller than array TTT, if, either:\n\n\nSSS is a prefix of TTT and ∣S∣&lt;∣T∣|S| \\lt |T|∣S∣&lt;∣T∣, or;\nIn the first position where SSS and TTT differ, array SSS has an element that is smaller than the corresponding element in array TTT.\nFor example, [1,2,3][1, 2, 3][1,2,3] is lexicographically smaller than [1,2,4],[1,2,3,4],[1, 2, 4], [1, 2, 3, 4],[1,2,4],[1,2,3,4], and [2][2][2].\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first line of each test case contains two positive integers NNN and QQQ, the number of nodes and the number of queries respectively.\nThe second line contains NNN space separated integers, A1,A2…ANA_1, A_2 \\ldots A_NA1​,A2​…AN​ −-− denoting the array AAA.\nThe following next N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two integers uuu and vvv, denoting an edge between nodes uuu and vvv. It is guaranteed that the given edges form a tree.\nThe following next QQQ lines contains two integers uuu and vvv, the nodes whose value should be swapped.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, print the sum of all u(1≤u≤N)u(1 \\leq u \\leq N)u(1≤u≤N) such that Pu=LP_u = LPu​=L.",
